message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it as below."
title: "pollination-morphology: mechanical isolation from computed pollen placement"
abstract: >-
  A simulation in which where a flower deposits pollen on a pollinator is
  computed from flower and body geometry rather than set as a trait, so that
  mechanical reproductive isolation can arise — or fail to — for inspectable
  reasons. Includes an individual-based model with inheritance and
  recombination, and pre-registered tests of temporal assortment, spatial
  structure, evolving flowering width, and reproductive assurance.
type: software
